# .claudeignore -- the enforced half of the asset-processing table's row 13
# ("VIP source -> NOT loaded into context, only symbol-indexed").
#
# Until 2026-09-04 no .claudeignore existed in this repo at all, so the
# context-budget tier-1 NEVER-VIP-SOURCE rule
# (dv_harness/context_budget.policy.json) was enforced only by the PreToolUse
# hook -- which, by its own documented limits, classifies literal paths only
# and fails open when Python is unavailable. This file is the second,
# independent layer.
#
# THE ROUTE FORWARD, whenever a pattern here blocks something you need:
#   1. `python -m dv_harness.vip_symbol_index` builds a symbol index of the
#      VIP source (class/method names + file:line, never bodies).
#   2. `vip_symbol_index.find_symbol(index, "<name>")` gives you the exact
#      file:line to read.
#   3. Read THAT one location. A single targeted read is a deliberate,
#      bounded exemption; paging the tree in is what this file prevents.
#   4. `docs/vip_ref/<protocol>.md`, generated by the same module, is the
#      tier-3 distilled reference to consult first.
#
# SCOPING NOTE (deliberate, do not "simplify" into bare directory patterns):
# every VIP pattern below is qualified by a SOURCE FILE EXTENSION rather than
# matching a `vip/` directory outright. This repo contains
# `.dv-harness/vault/03_Verification/VIP/`, which is Obsidian verification-
# knowledge markdown -- real, intentionally readable content that a bare
# `**/vip/` pattern would wrongly hide. Extension-qualified patterns cannot
# match those .md notes.

# --- VIP source trees (tier 1: NEVER-VIP-SOURCE) ---
**/vip/**/*.sv
**/vip/**/*.svh
**/vip/**/*.svp
**/vip/**/*.vp
**/vip/**/*.v
**/vip/**/*.vh
**/svt_*/**/*.sv
**/svt_*/**/*.svh
**/designware/**/*.sv
**/designware/**/*.svh

# Deliberate carve-out, matching context_budget.policy.json's own allow_globs:
# VIP Examples/ reference testbenches and .f filelists stay readable. They are
# the sanctioned reference material for branch-B/VIP-driven work, and denying
# them is the false positive that gets a gate switched off entirely.
!**/vip/examples/**
!**/vip/Examples/**
!**/vip/**/*.f

# --- Raw PDF originals (tier 1: NEVER-RAW-PDF) ---
# Distil with dv_harness/doc_extraction.py, then read the distillate.
**/*.pdf

# --- Whole-chip design/waveform/evidence databases (tier 1: NEVER-WHOLE-CHIP-DB) ---
# Query these (fsdb_report.py, the query_regression MCP verb); never stream them.
**/*.fsdb
**/*.vpd
**/*.vcd
**/*.trn
**/simv.daidir/**
**/csrc/**
**/novas_dump.log

# --- Complete simulation / regression logs (tier 1: NEVER-REGRESSION-LOGS) ---
# Distil with dv_harness/sim_log_analysis.py; the engineering content is a
# handful of UVM_ERROR lines and a verdict, which the analyser already extracts.
**/sim.log
**/simv.log
**/comp.log
**/compile.log
**/elab.log
